db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d718b4fe-ac83-5ded-9cff-9bf61a11c436" :question/math-academy-id "q-14238" :question/problem "Find $k$ if $2$ is a root of $f(x)={x}^{4}+k{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-57x+6k.$" :question/worked-solution "Since  $x=2$ is a root, we have $f(2)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=2,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{4}+k(2)^{3}-7(2)^{2}-57(2)+6k & =0 \\\\ 16+8k-28-114+6k & =0 \\\\ 14k-126 & =0 \\\\ 14k & =126 \\\\ k & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
